{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact15680192f93b6268f405b52b21ce0874060bc193 for overhead request ecbc722a. All180 current artifacts are cited, with reporting primary a803de1f first. This reviews the overhead delta relative to composed baseline a1990c94; it does not approve inherited Stage2/3/5/MCP implementations. Actual focused evidence is in git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d7ccc8f09ee153631fc7be034a329a6ff144769 and its two immutable JSON attachments.\n\nP2 — Complete the promised affected-test selection. scripts/test-changed.mjs:50 recognizes a root lock/tsconfig change, but line67 still invokes root Vitest only with --changed. On installed Vitest4.1.11, an isolated baseline witness passes; lock-only and root-tsconfig-only changes then select no root tests, exit0 and report root passed while the Git/UI fixture runners run. These global triggers must select the whole root suite. Also, lines32–34 split Git's quoted newline paths and line53 compares them with unquoted package prefixes: an actual untracked Unicode UI test is missed and UI is reported unaffected. Discover NUL-delimited paths and handle paths the underlying Vitest changed reader cannot decode, or use a bounded conservative whole-project fallback. Ordinary package/dependency closures are supported; no new selector framework or exhaustive case matrix is requested.\n\nP2 — Keep invalid control runs inconclusive. Exact control.mjs SHA256c29bac9b85aa8b3483b54ce8c91d8de6a7c115bfee969ba120128245ec9dd626 was exercised unchanged with small actual Node-runner fixtures. Passing baseline→named assertion correctly exits0; passing baseline→plain thrown error correctly exits2. But after all tests are skipped it exits1 SURVIVES with0pass/0fail, and a named assertion plus a separate test timeout exits0 DISTINGUISHES. Detect no-executed-test and timeout/infrastructure results before granting the machine verdict. A genuine observed assertion may be retained as partial evidence;